Not physically. Not violently. But like ink dissolving in water—the rough wood of the inn’s walls softened, peeled back in translucent layers, revealing not brick or beam, but *memory*: flickering images of hands placing coins in offering bowls, children tracing runes on cobblestones, a lone knight kneeling before a shrine, whispering vows long forgotten.

